  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity-building Support to the Government of Philippines for Improved Emergency Preparedness and Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Philippines is one of the most high-risk countries in the world in terms of frequency and intensity of natural hazards. It ranked number one globally in the 2022 World Risk Index due to the country&#x2019;s high risk, exposure, and vulnerability to climate change. The country has been experiencing more and more extreme weather events with increased ferocity due to climate change, and typhoons are becoming more intense and destructive. Strong typhoons most frequently hit Bicol Region, Visayas and Northern Luzon, according to Manila Observatory. 
 
The proposed initiatives in this project aims to address the systematic needs and build the institutional capacities of the Department of Humanitarian Settlement and Urban Development (DHSUD), the Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD), and relevant local government leaders to further improve the Government&#x2019;s disaster preparedness and response, especially in the areas of Shelter and Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) planning and response, data and information management, and coordination.</narrative>
  </description>
